 "findings": [
  {
   "finding_id": "W1-001",
   "severity": "medium",
   "items": [
    "D-162",
    "D-149",
    "D-148"
   ],
   "claim": "The 'Logger shutdown' decision closes the app logger 'as the last step of D-162'. Frozen D-162 puts 'flushing and closing log writers' before 'the adapter release of D-107 and the move to TERMINATED', so 'last step' moves the logger close after the adapter release and contradicts the frozen order. The round-2 fix asked for the logger close in D-162's own log-writer step, after the owned resources close and before the adapter release. The decision also moves the close of a logger passed to ctx.own(...) or registered out of its D-149 reverse-order position without saying so.",
   "evidence": "docs/research/naruserve-v1/waves/wave-4/design.md:130; docs/research/naruserve-v1/waves/wave-4/design.md:78 (D-162); docs/research/naruserve-v1/waves/wave-4/rounds/r2-merged.json W1-002/W2-002 suggested_fix",
   "suggested_fix": "Replace 'As the last step of D-162' with 'In D-162's flushing-and-closing-log-writers step (after owned and registered resources are closed, before the adapter release)'. State that a logger that is also owned or registered is skipped in the D-149 reverse-order pass and closed once in that step."
  },
  {
   "finding_id": "W1-002",
   "severity": "low",
   "items": [
    "D-226",
    "D-227"
   ],
   "claim": "The 'RestApp.create()' decision tests the ServiceLoader lookup 'with a test-fixtures factory and with none'. NaruServe-api applies java-test-fixtures, and its own test classpath plus every consumer of testFixtures (later bootstrap and adapter modules) includes the fixtures. If the fixture factory is registered through META-INF/services in testFixtures, the 'none' case cannot be observed in the same test JVM, and in wave 5 the real bootstrap factory would sit beside the fixture factory, which gives two providers. The decision says nothing about how this is kept apart. The interface name and the services path are also still left open (r2 W2-005).",
   "evidence": "docs/research/naruserve-v1/waves/wave-4/design.md:128; build.gradle:166 (java-test-fixtures), build.gradle:255 (testFixturesJar consumed)",
   "suggested_fix": "Register the test factory only in NaruServe-api's test source set, or load it through a dedicated ClassLoader in the test, and not in testFixtures. Name the factory interface and its META-INF/services path in docs/api/app.md when it is decided."
  }
 ]
